        "position": "inside-top-left",
        "wWidth": 700,
        "description": "<p>The four versions differ in two transformations that the compiler can do:</p><p>&bull; <b>Vectorization</b> (SIMD): one instruction processes 4 doubles at once, in a 256-bit register (AVX2, enabled by <i>-march=native</i>). <i>-fno-tree-vectorize</i> disables it.<br>&bull; <b>Unrolling with several accumulators</b>: <i>-funroll-loops</i> (at most 4 times) and <i>-fvariable-expansion-in-unroller</i> split the sum S into 4 partial sums, which are added after the loop.</p><p><i>-Ofast</i> lets the compiler change the order of the floating-point additions: both transformations need it.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:4px 0\"><tr><th style=\"text-align:left;padding:2px 10px\">Program</th><th style=\"padding:2px 10px\">SIMD</th><th style=\"padding:2px 10px\">Accumulators</th><th style=\"padding:2px 10px\">Elements per iteration (S)</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\"><b>SUM-scalar</b></td><td style=\"text-align:center\">no</td><td style=\"text-align:center\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\"><b>SUM-simd</b></td><td style=\"text-align:center\">4 doubles</td><td style=\"text-align:center\">1 (vector)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\"><b>SUM-scalar4</b></td><td style=\"text-align:center\">no</td><td style=\"text-align:center\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\"><b>SUM-simd4</b></td><td style=\"text-align:center\">4 doubles</td><td style=\"text-align:center\">4 (vectors)</td><td style=\"text-align:center\">16</td></tr></table><p>The next cards show the machine code (x86-64) of each loop and its RVCAT program.</p>",
        "next": [
          "p-scalar"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p-scalar",
        "type": "step",
        "title": "SUM-scalar",
        "anchor": "#right-panel",
        "position": "inside-top-left",
        "wWidth": 700,
        "description": "<p><i>gcc -Ofast -fno-tree-vectorize -march=native</i>: no vectorization, but gcc unrolls the loop 2 times by itself.</p><pre>f0: vaddsd  (%rax),%xmm0,%xmm0      # S = S + V[i]     (load + add)\n    add     $0x10,%rax              # i = i + 2        (16 bytes)\n    vaddsd  -0x8(%rax),%xmm0,%xmm0  # S = S + V[i-1]   (load + add)\n    cmp     %rax,%rcx               # c = i != N\n    jne     f0                      # if c go back</pre><p>x86-64 adds an operand read from memory: each <i>vaddsd</i> is a <b>load</b> and an <b>addition</b>, two rows of RVCAT. The loop has <b>7 instructions</b> and adds <b>2 elements</b> per iteration (S = 2), with a single accumulator S: <b>2 dependent additions</b> per iteration.</p>",
        "actions": [
          "selectProgram:SUM-scalar",
          "switchTo:simulationComponent",
          "programView:type"
        ],
        "next": [
          "p-simd"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p-simd",
        "type": "step",
        "title": "SUM-simd",
        "anchor": "#right-panel",
        "position": "inside-top-left",
        "wWidth": 700,
        "description": "<p><i>gcc -Ofast -march=native</i>: the loop is <b>vectorized</b>. <i>vaddpd</i> on a 256-bit register (ymm) adds <b>4 doubles</b> at once.</p><pre>110: vaddpd (%rax),%ymm0,%ymm0       # S[0:3] = S[0:3] + V[i:i+3]  (load + add)\n     add    $0x20,%rax               # i = i + 4        (32 bytes)\n     cmp    %rax,%rdx                # c = i != N\n     jne    110                      # if c go back</pre><p>RVCAT program: a vector load of 4 doubles, a vector addition, and the loop control: <b>5 instructions</b>, <b>4 elements</b> per iteration (S = 4). The accumulator S[0:3] keeps 4 partial sums (one per lane), which are added after the loop.</p>",
        "actions": [
          "selectProgram:SUM-simd",
          "switchTo:simulationComponent",
          "programView:type"
        ],
        "next": [
          "p-scalar4"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p-scalar4",
        "type": "step",
        "title": "SUM-scalar4",
        "anchor": "#right-panel",
        "position": "inside-top-left",
        "wWidth": 700,
        "description": "<p>Unrolled 4 times, with <b>4 accumulators</b> (S0 to S3, variable expansion), and not vectorized.</p><pre>1b3: vaddsd (%r8),%xmm1,%xmm1        # S0 = S0 + V[i]\n     vaddsd 0x8(%r8),%xmm4,%xmm4     # S1 = S1 + V[i+1]\n     add    $0x20,%r8                # i = i + 4        (32 bytes)\n     vaddsd -0x10(%r8),%xmm2,%xmm2   # S2 = S2 + V[i+2]\n     vaddsd -0x8(%r8),%xmm3,%xmm3    # S3 = S3 + V[i+3]\n     cmp    %r12,%r8                 # c = i != N\n     jne    1b3                      # if c go back</pre><p>RVCAT program: <b>11 instructions</b>, <b>4 elements</b> per iteration (S = 4), and <b>4 independent chains of additions</b> instead of one.</p>",
        "actions": [
          "selectProgram:SUM-scalar4",
          "switchTo:simulationComponent",
          "programView:type"
        ],
        "next": [
          "p-simd4"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p-simd4",
        "type": "step",
        "title": "SUM-simd4",
        "anchor": "#right-panel",
        "position": "inside-top-left",
        "wWidth": 700,
        "description": "<p>Vectorized and unrolled 4 times, with <b>4 vector accumulators</b> of 4 doubles each.</p><pre>1ec: vaddpd (%r11),%ymm1,%ymm1           # S0[0:3] += V[i:i+3]\n     vaddpd 0x20(%r11),%ymm4,%ymm4       # S1[0:3] += V[i+4:i+7]\n     sub    $0xffffffffffffff80,%r11     # i = i + 16       (+128 bytes)\n     vaddpd -0x40(%r11),%ymm2,%ymm2      # S2[0:3] += V[i+8:i+11]\n     vaddpd -0x20(%r11),%ymm3,%ymm3      # S3[0:3] += V[i+12:i+15]\n     cmp    %r11,%rsi                    # c = i != N\n     jne    1ec                          # if c go back</pre><p>RVCAT program: <b>11 instructions</b>, <b>16 elements</b> per iteration (S = 16): each iteration reads 16 × 8 = <b>128 bytes</b> of V.</p>",
        "actions": [
          "selectProgram:SUM-simd4",
          "switchTo:simulationComponent",
          "programView:type"
        ],
        "next": [
          "cache"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "cache",
        "type": "step",
        "title": "The processor and its cache",
        "selector": "#process-panel .processor-container",
        "anchor": "#right-panel",
        "position": "inside-top-left",
        "wWidth": 700,
        "description": "<p>The processor <b>GC-16</b> is configured like an Intel <b>Golden Cove</b> core: up to 6 instructions dispatched and 8 retired per cycle, a ROB of 200 entries, and 10 execution ports (3 of them for loads and 2 for stores).</p><p>Its <b><span style=\"color:#c62828\">cache</span></b> is very small, so that its effect is easy to see: <b>16 blocks of 64 bytes</b> (1 KB). A block holds 64 / 8 = <b>8 doubles</b>. The data that are not in the cache come from the <b>main memory</b>, block by block (a <b>cache miss</b>).</p><p>With N = 1,024, the vector V takes 8 KB: <b>128 blocks</b>, much more than the cache. Each block of V is read once, so each one is a miss.</p>",
        "actions": [
          "reveal:processor",
          "sidePanel:show"
        ],
        "next": [
          "q-blocks"
        ]
      },
      {
